WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.234
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:04.367
Wow!
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:07.133
That was great.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:10.367
I'd like to start by wishing
everybody a happy New Year.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:11.667
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:14.400
♪♪

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.634
Happy New Year.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:19.467
I can already tell 2022
is gonna be better than 2021,

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.033
mostly because it's impossible
for it to not be.

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:25.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.400
According to a new poll,
Americans say the one word

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.901
that best describes their mood
about 2022 is "hopeful."

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.067
-Yeah!
-Then 2021 heard that and was

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.267
like, "Yeah,
good luck with that."

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.434
[ Imitates puffing
on cigarette ]

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:39.167
It's amazing
how much life has changed.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.901
In just two years,
our resolutions went from

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:43.734
"run a marathon" to "only spend
four hours a day on TikTok."

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.234
[ Laughter ]
That's your...

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:46.834
This year, my New Year's
resolution is to have

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:50.067
more self-confidence, but I just
know I'll screw it up somehow.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.367
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.400
I like having New Year's
resolutions because you can just

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.934
make them up as you go, sort of
like the CDC rules on COVID.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:59.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:04.901
Five days, four days,
three days...

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:07.567
Speaking of New Year's,
I saw that Jeff Bezos celebrated

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.167
at a '70s-themed disco party,

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.667
and he definitely
dressed the part.

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.133
Here's a photo.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:14.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:17.334
Look at those pants!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.667
As they say over at Amazon,
that's a tight package.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:25.200
-Oy!
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.267
Whoa-ho.
-Well, today President Biden

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.734
flew into Washington, D.C.,
from Delaware,

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.734
right as a major snowstorm
was hitting,

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:35.767
and when he landed, he actually
got stuck on Air Force One

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:38.701
'cause they had trouble driving
the stairs over to the plane.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.767
Check this out.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:44.534
-Ooh, come on.
[ Grunts ]

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:47.968
Mm, mm.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:51.000
Yeah.
Whew, man, we were this close

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.667
to seeing the president
of the United States

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.467
jump down an inflatable slide.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:57.467
That would have been so --
This close.

00:01:57.467 --> 00:02:02.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.801
Can we see that again?

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.601
I'd like to look at
the video again because I love

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.901
the two guys off to the side,
watching.

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:09.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.734
Standing there, watching,
pushing a giant stair.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:12.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:14.934
"Yeah, good job.
You're doing a good job.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.567
Good work."

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.968
Thankfully, Biden finally did
make it off the plane.

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:22.467
Here he is walking out.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.300
Yeah.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.834
That's right.
The last time D.C. was hit

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.133
with that much whiteness,
it was January 6th.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:31.100
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]
[ Applause ]

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:35.033
[ Rimshot ]
Coming in hot!

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:39.167
Coming back hot!
Coming back hot!

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.234
With the retweetable jokes.
There you go.

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:42.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:44.667
Seriously, there hasn't been
that much white powder

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.934
since Jeff Bezos's
New Year's party.

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:50.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:53.267
Come on.
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:55.834
If you're keeping track,
Biden can somehow walk down

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.567
a flight of icy stairs
in the snow

00:02:57.567 --> 00:03:00.167
but not up a flight of stairs
when it's nice out.

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:01.334
Watch this.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:04.601
-Oh. Oh!
-Oh, boy!

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:05.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:08.200
The third one is the one
that gets you, yeah.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.601
Some more travel problems.
This weekend, over 5,000 flights

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.100
were cancelled,
largely due to COVID.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.767
Yep, airlines are having a tough
time staffing their flights.

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:17.834
You can tell.
Just listen to this

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:19.334
captain's announcement I heard.

00:03:47.968 --> 00:03:49.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
Wow.

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:52.834
Rolling the dice --
Wow. Interesting.

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:55.968
-Wow.
[ Laughing ]

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.267
-Now, speaking of COVID,
the CDC recently issued

00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:00.133
a warning to avoid cruise ships,

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:03.033
regardless
of vaccination status.

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.501
I'm sorry,
that was news from 2018.

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:07.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.501
Hey, on the other hand, though,
you book a one-week cruise

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:12.534
and test positive, you got
yourself a three-week cruise.

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:13.934
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:15.868
Think about it.

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:19.834
You got to do the math.

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:22.000
Meanwhile, the CDC has cut
their recommended

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.701
isolation time in half,
and now it says you only need

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:26.801
to quarantine for five days.

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:29.000
Yeah, a lot of COVID regulations
keep changing

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.100
the longer the pandemic goes on.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.033
For example, back then,
doctors said

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:34.934
to cough directly
into your elbow.

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:37.133
Now doctors say,
"Just have fun out there."

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:38.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:39.200
I don't know what that means.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.167
[ Applause ]

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:43.567
Here's another example.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:47.200
Then, the CDC said to avoid
large indoor gatherings.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.901
Now the CDC says
parties are fine so long as you

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.868
set up a smaller,
"tested positive" table.

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:56.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:58.934
Also, back then,
you had to wash your hands

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:02.067
for as long as it takes to sing
"Happy Birthday" twice.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:04.767
But now you can sing it at the
speed Applebee's employees do

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:06.501
when you can tell
they're not really into it.

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:07.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:09.467
♪ Happy birthday,
happy birthday ♪

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:12.567
♪ I brought bread,
here whatever ♪

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:14.801
And finally, back then,
they said to avoid

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:17.200
misinformation by staying off
the Internet,

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.534
but now the Internet
is where you live now.

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:21.400
It is your home.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.000
That's interesting.
A lot has changed.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:27.467
-Wow.

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:30.734
-Well, some news from overseas.
Yesterday, South Korea said that

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:35.400
an unidentified person crossed
the border into North Korea.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.534
Really?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:39.067
It's like running
out of Disneyland

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:40.801
and into...North Korea.

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:42.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:44.801
I can't think of anything worse.

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.133
Well, everyone
is talking about this.

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:48.567
In the middle of the
Jets/Buccaneers game yesterday,

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:50.734
Tampa Bay wide receiver
Antonio --

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:53.567
You knew I had to talk about it.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:56.367
Antonio Brown got a little upset
and decided to leave the game.

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:57.767
Take a look at this.

00:05:57.767 --> 00:06:00.968
-Antonio Brown boiled over.
Very upset on the sidelines.

00:06:00.968 --> 00:06:04.267
Took off his shoulder pads.
He tossed his shoulder pads,

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:05.567
stripped off his shirt
and glove,

00:06:05.567 --> 00:06:08.901
threw those into the crowd,
then ran across the field

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.434
while the teams
were still on the field,

00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:12.934
giving the crowd
a peace-out sign.

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:14.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.367 --> 00:06:16.300
-Before you judge him,
that's the same way

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:18.334
Andy Cohen
left Times Square on Saturday.

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:23.367
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:25.200
-Oh!
-Andy was great.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.434
-Oh, boy.

00:06:27.434 --> 00:06:29.033
-I have a feeling,
after one more variant,

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.167
that's exactly how Dr. Fauci
is gonna say goodbye.

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:35.334
He's gonna be like, "I'm out!"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:37.467
And, finally,
a woman chose to quarantine

00:06:37.467 --> 00:06:39.968
in an airplane bathroom
for three hours

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:43.701
after she tested positive
for COVID mid-flight.

00:06:43.701 --> 00:06:45.133
It wasn't really a tough choice.

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:47.167
It was either that
or the overhead bin.

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:49.467
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:51.133
Meanwhile, a second passenger
spent three hours

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:53.300
in the other bathroom
after testing positive

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.634
for the hummus wrap.

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:57.567
-Happy New Year, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:57.567 --> 00:07:01.334
It is Monday.
We're so excited to be back!

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:04.133
And we're kicking off 2022
with a great week of shows.

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:06.434
Cate Blanchett will be here.
Kenan Thompson.

00:07:06.434 --> 00:07:08.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
Milo Ventimiglia.

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:10.234
And the co-hosts of "Queer Eye"

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:11.767
will all be joining us
this week.

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:13.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:15.467
But first, what a show
we have for you tonight.

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:17.801
He stars in the series
"Black-ish."

00:07:17.801 --> 00:07:20.334
The final season premieres --
I know, we love him.

00:07:20.334 --> 00:07:22.934
The final season premieres
tomorrow night, on ABC.

00:07:22.934 --> 00:07:25.567
The very funny Anthony Anderson
is here tonight.

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:28.868
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:07:28.868 --> 00:07:31.133
Plus, you can see him
in the HBO series

00:07:31.133 --> 00:07:34.734
"The Righteous Gemstones."
Adam Devine is joining us.

00:07:34.734 --> 00:07:36.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.634
Adam's very funny.
And we've got great music,

00:07:38.634 --> 00:07:41.367
great, great music
from Carly Pearce, everybody!

00:07:41.367 --> 00:07:43.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:47.434
Carly Pearce.

00:07:47.434 --> 00:07:49.634
I hope everyone
had a good break.

00:07:49.634 --> 00:07:54.934
We were off for two weeks,
and we double taped on Thursday,

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:57.734
and we had Friday off.
On Saturday, I was gonna come in

00:07:57.734 --> 00:07:59.567
and do a bit
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:07:59.567 --> 00:08:02.567
-Yep.
-And I tested positive.

00:08:02.567 --> 00:08:05.400
But I was so scared,
because I went in --

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:06.934
You know, I normally come in.
I've been here --

00:08:06.934 --> 00:08:09.734
We've been doing this testing
for over a year now maybe.

00:08:09.734 --> 00:08:11.200
So I know everyone up there,

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.801
all the nurses and doctors
and everyone.

00:08:12.801 --> 00:08:15.200
So I'm standing there
with the security guard

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.868
and some producers
for "Saturday Night Live"

00:08:16.868 --> 00:08:20.100
and my assistant,
and the nurse comes back in.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:23.534
She goes, "Come with me."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:25.200
I've never gotten --
I know, I've never gotten,

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.767
"Come with me."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.767 --> 00:08:28.367
"Come with me"?
I go, "Wow.

00:08:28.367 --> 00:08:30.868
You gotta be kidding me.
I mean, we test every day here."

00:08:30.868 --> 00:08:32.901
-Yeah.
-And I wash my hands,

00:08:32.901 --> 00:08:35.267
I do everything, I wear a mask.

00:08:35.267 --> 00:08:38.367
Anyways, they put me in a --
like, a waiting area.

00:08:38.367 --> 00:08:41.634
And it's like a glass --
a glass office, maybe?

00:08:41.634 --> 00:08:44.133
-Yeah.
-It's a tiny desk and a phone,

00:08:44.133 --> 00:08:46.100
and you're in --
and they shut me in there.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:49.100
And they said,
"Someone's gonna call you."

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.968
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.968 --> 00:08:52.234
Yeah.
And they left, and I said,

00:08:52.234 --> 00:08:54.601
"Oh, man, this is bizarre.
This is sad."

00:08:54.601 --> 00:08:56.167
So I texted my assistant
and said,

00:08:56.167 --> 00:08:58.868
"Please take a photo of me
in this room."

00:08:58.868 --> 00:09:00.567
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.567 --> 00:09:02.434
And so this is me,
and this is true --

00:09:02.434 --> 00:09:05.167
this is really me in the waiting
area, if you can see this.

00:09:05.167 --> 00:09:07.601
That's me there.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.601 --> 00:09:09.434
Wait. So, wait.
So this is --

00:09:09.434 --> 00:09:12.100
So this is real deal.
I'm not even joking.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:13.534
That's where they put you.
You know that room?

00:09:13.534 --> 00:09:15.501
-I hang in there all the time.
-No, that's the COVID room.

00:09:15.501 --> 00:09:17.100
You can't hang out there.
-I didn't know that.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.934
-We've hung out there before.
-Yes.

00:09:18.934 --> 00:09:20.701
-So they put me in this room,
right?

00:09:20.701 --> 00:09:25.000
So every office has
a catch phrase from an NBC show,

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:28.000
like from "Cheers" or something,
or "Here's Johnny."

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:31.767
I'm not kidding.
The room I'm in is the

00:09:31.767 --> 00:09:33.400
"What'chu talking 'bout,
Willis" room.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:38.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:38.767 --> 00:09:41.334
I zoomed in.
I zoomed in so you can see that.

00:09:41.334 --> 00:09:43.868
I can't --
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.868 --> 00:09:45.534
That's where I found out --

00:09:45.534 --> 00:09:47.667
that's where I found out
that I had COVID.

00:09:47.667 --> 00:09:49.033
Yeah, that was the room.

00:09:49.033 --> 00:09:50.501
That was the place
where I found out.

00:09:50.501 --> 00:09:52.067
You can't write this,
you can't make it up.

00:09:52.067 --> 00:09:53.901
-You were only there for like
an hour and a half, right?

00:09:53.901 --> 00:09:57.100
-That's all, yeah.
So then, I call my wife.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:59.667
You know, I go --
you know, we had to isolate,

00:09:59.667 --> 00:10:01.367
and it's right before Christmas.

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:02.701
I go,
"Man, this is gonna be crazy.

00:10:02.701 --> 00:10:04.868
What am I gonna do?"
So --

00:10:04.868 --> 00:10:08.534
You know, but --
So they went Upstate

00:10:08.534 --> 00:10:10.400
with the girls, you know,
and I just kind of sat there,

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:11.634
just isolated.
You know, I just did what --

00:10:11.634 --> 00:10:14.033
You know, just --
You know, I just ordered

00:10:14.033 --> 00:10:15.434
delivery, they dropped it
outside the door.

00:10:15.434 --> 00:10:17.767
You know, whatever.
And then I said,

00:10:17.767 --> 00:10:19.000
"You should have
the girls tested,

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.501
and you guys should test again,"
and they tested --

00:10:20.501 --> 00:10:22.667
My girls tested positive,
as well.

00:10:22.667 --> 00:10:24.367
[ Audience "Awws" ]
And they're fine.

00:10:24.367 --> 00:10:25.701
Everyone's fine.
They had the sniffles.

00:10:25.701 --> 00:10:27.901
Frannie had sniffles
for like two days.

00:10:27.901 --> 00:10:29.801
Winnie had no symptoms at all.

00:10:29.801 --> 00:10:32.934
But that meant I could go home.

00:10:32.934 --> 00:10:35.601
And spend the holidays
with the kids, so I did.

00:10:35.601 --> 00:10:37.133
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:10:37.133 --> 00:10:40.801
It was a Christmas miracle.

00:10:40.801 --> 00:10:43.267
But anyways, it was --
I want to just tell everyone,

00:10:43.267 --> 00:10:45.767
please, out there,
get vaxxed, if you can.

00:10:45.767 --> 00:10:48.334
Get vaxxed, get boosted,
because, man, this thing,

00:10:48.334 --> 00:10:50.701
it's a banger.
It's a real thing.

00:10:50.701 --> 00:10:54.767
If I didn't have that, I know,
it just felt like I would be

00:10:54.767 --> 00:10:57.100
real, real, real, real, sick.
So I want to thank

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.367
all of my doctors
for giving me the vax

